('30-year mortgage rates are 6.22-6.45%, up from 5.87% in February.','30-year mortgage rates are sitting','PMMS2026: Freddie Mac 6.22% (19 March) and 6.38% (26 March); the February low was 5.98% (26 February). The 5.87% baseline is not supported by Freddie Mac; it may come from a daily index not checked. Partly correct.',['PMMS2026']),
('Americans carry $1.277 trillion in credit card debt; card APRs 21-24%.','$1.277\ntrillion in credit card debt','NYFEDQ4: New York Fed Q4 2025 credit card balances $1.28 trillion (released 10 February 2026). Verified. APR range not fetched.',['NYFEDQ4']),
('"Our research tracking over a million investor accounts" found the average equity investor underperformed the S&P 500 for 15 consecutive years, by almost 850 basis points in 2024.','Our research tracking over a\nmillion investor accounts','DALBAR2025: DALBAR QAIB 2025 reports 16.54% vs 25.02% in 2024 (848 bp) and 15 consecutive years of underperformance. The figures are verified, but the first-person "our research" presents a third-party study as the creator\'s own, an attribution problem. DALBAR methodology uses fund flows, not tracked individual accounts.',['DALBAR2025']),
('Seven of the 10 best days over 20 years were in bear markets, six within two weeks of the worst days; missing the 10 best days each decade since 1930 turns ~15,000% into 91%.','seven of the\n10 best trading days','Resembles J.P. Morgan Guide to Retirement and Hartford Funds statistics (analyst recall). The specific 15,000% vs 91% pair was not found in search, and Hartford versions recalled by the analyst use different figures. '+U,[]),
('High-yield savings pay 4-4.2%, ten times the 0.39% national average; paying off a 22% card is a guaranteed 22% return.','10 times the national average','K02: 4.0/0.39 = 10.3x and 4.2/0.39 = 10.8x (reproduce). The FDIC national rate was not fetched. The 22% equivalence is approximately right as an avoided-interest return (not literally tax-free income). K02: $3,800 at 22% = $836/year interest; $900 charged at 22% for 8 months = about $141 interest.',[]),
