TITLE='Authentic title "Are You Ready For What\'s Coming?" is a vague threat/curiosity frame with no number or topic noun; the script fills it with a five-wave household impact model of the March 2026 Iran war oil shock. It is the cohort\'s clear outlier (STRONG), released while the shock dominated news. Peers are evergreen money-mindset titles. Association only; no CTR or experiment evidence.'
THUMB='Registered maxresdefault 1280x720 (HTTP 200, real image). White field. Left: the recurring cartoon man in a grey T-shirt, eyes wide, mouth open. Centre: a red zig-zag arrow plunging across a candlestick chart. Right: a black two-line headline "IT\'S COMING" with a curved black arrow pointing back at the chart. The thumbnail signals a market drop; the script is about consumer prices and rates and tells viewers not to sell. At 320x180 the headline, face and red arrow remain legible; candlesticks become texture.'
SCRIPT='A news-driven explainer: delayed-cost hook, timeline of the 28 February 2026 strikes and Hormuz closure, IEA response and oil prices, two composite households (Maya; Ryan and Jess), five waves (gas, groceries, fertilizer, airfare, interest rates), an investor-behaviour section (DALBAR, best days), five actions (emergency fund in high-yield savings, attack card debt, keep investing, book flights, audit energy exposure), two scenarios and a close. Verified: IEA record 400M barrel release and "largest disruption", Brent ~$120 peak, late-March gas/diesel levels, Fed hold at 3.50-3.75%, $1.28T card debt, DALBAR 848 bp/15 years, urea +~50% and Hormuz third of urea trade, jet fuel ~+58% week. Wrong or unsupported: 5.87% February mortgage baseline (Freddie 5.98%), "32% in a single week" NOLA, Spirit 124%, 15,000% vs 91%, "1973 and 1979 combined". Attribution problem: DALBAR research described as "our research". The Maya grocery example (+12-21%) overstates the 4.4% CPI projection. The stored ending is complete.'
BEATS=['Hook: costs arriving months after 28 February.','Intro and promise of five waves.','Timeline: talks, strikes, retaliation, Hormuz closure, IEA release, oil prices.','Two households introduced.','Wave 1: gasoline and diesel.','Wave 2: groceries via diesel freight.','Wave 3: fertilizer and the October harvest.','Aside: waves 1-3 hit everyone.','Wave 4: airfare.','Wave 5: Fed and interest rates.','Investor behaviour: DALBAR and best days.','Five actions.','Two scenarios and close.']
